# Nougat OCR extraction — stub

This replication of arXiv:2003.02417 (Nakaji, *Faster Amplitude Estimation*) did NOT run nougat / marker OCR
on the paper PDF. The clean-room reimplementation of Algorithm 1 was performed by reading
`work/paper.txt` (produced by `pdftotext work/paper.pdf work/paper.txt`) and the extracted figure
`work/img-004.png` (produced by `pdfimages -png work/paper.pdf img`).

For OCR-based extraction (equation reconstruction, table parsing, cross-reference resolution), rerun with
either nougat or marker; suggested command:

    marker_single work/paper.pdf extraction/ --extract_images

The paper is 12 pages, mostly clean LaTeX-rendered PDF, so `pdftotext` output was sufficient to
reconstruct:

- Algorithm 1 pseudocode (§2.3)
- eq. (5): definition of Q = X S_0 X^† S_good
- eq. (8): Chernoff interval [cos^(-)_m, cos^(+)_m]
- eq. (9): extended atan2 for stage-2 sign resolution
- eq. (10): trig-addition identity for sin reconstruction
- eq. (24)–(25): integer n_j update rule
- eq. (28): proven prefactor 4.1 × 10^3 for N_orac upper bound
- §2.3 shot-count constants: N_shot^{1st} = 1944 · ln(2/δ_c), N_shot^{2nd} = 972 · ln(2/δ_c)
- Fig. 3 numerical setup: a ∈ {0.1, 0.2, 0.3, 0.4}, 1000 trials per (a, ℓ), 95th-percentile amplitude
  error

No equation was misread; the machine-precision agreement of oracle.py's `exact_prob_good_after_Qm`
with the analytic identity sin²((2m+1)θ) is direct evidence that eq. (5) was read correctly.
